# Text files are normalised to LF, on checkout, on every platform — the
# git blobs are already all LF, but Windows git defaults core.autocrlf=true
# and silently rewrites the working tree to CRLF on checkout, which made
# `prettier --check` (endOfLine defaults to "lf") flag every single file on
# windows-latest CI runners.
* text=auto eol=lf

# DOCX fixtures are binary; never normalise line endings or diff them.
# The roundtrip gate (#8) asserts byte fidelity, which any filtering breaks.
# Listed after the blanket text rule above so its `binary` (implying -text)
# wins for these paths specifically — .gitattributes rules are applied in
# file order, last match takes precedence.
*.docx binary
